The four AXI adapters are 40.9% of this design's logic, 57.3% with the DMA load
unit. The 64-PE spatial array, at the 1,324.28 um2/PE measured on the T=4 designs,
would be about 3.7%. So the 4.33x is not compute: it is memory-interface mass that
Gemmini's TileLink path does not produce -- its reader, writer and transaction
tracker together are 23,885 um2, 6.3% of its logic.

Other readings:
- Against its own with-memory run (2,833,543.92): the two stubbed arrays are 19.8%
  of the full figure, against 53.9% for Gemmini at DIM=8. Their design is far more
  memory-dominated once memories become flip-flops, which is why the full-design
  ratio (2.49x) understates the logic difference and the logic-only ratio is the
  one to quote.
- Against our T=4 MAXDIM=64 logic-only (1,396,966.00): +62.7% for doubling T. Not
  a clean single-variable delta -- that run is a QD=8 export from allo 6db2dc7a -
  so it bounds the T=4-to-8 logic cost rather than measuring it.
- Non-combinational 79.6%, against 80.1% with memories in and ~80% in every
  TinyTPU run. Gemmini's logic-only share is 37.2%. Gate-heavy against flop-heavy,
  unchanged by array size, memory treatment or queue depth.
